# UI Policy Documentation

## Project Title

**Implement Client Script & UI Policy on ServiceNow Incident**

---

## 1. Introduction

A UI Policy in ServiceNow is used to dynamically control the behavior of form fields based on specified conditions. It can make fields mandatory, read-only, or visible without requiring the user to manually change the field properties.

In this project, a UI Policy is implemented on the **Incident** table to improve data entry and maintain consistent information while creating or updating Incident records.

The UI Policy works together with Client Scripts to provide dynamic form behavior and validation.

---

## 2. Objective

The main objectives of implementing the UI Policy are:

- To control Incident form fields dynamically.
- To make required fields mandatory when necessary.
- To make selected fields read-only based on conditions.
- To control the visibility of fields.
- To reduce incorrect or incomplete data entry.
- To improve consistency in Incident records.
- To provide a better user experience while working with Incident forms.

---

## 3. ServiceNow Table Used

The UI Policy is configured for the:

**Table:** Incident  
**Application:** ServiceNow Incident Management

The Incident table contains information related to reported issues, their priority, impact, state, category, assignment, and resolution.

