5. UI Policy Configuration

The UI Policy is created from the ServiceNow Incident module.

General Configuration

The following basic configuration is used:

Property	Description
Table	Incident
Active	Enabled
Condition	Defined based on the project requirement
UI Type	Applicable Incident form UI
Reverse if false	Used when the field behavior must return to its original state when the condition becomes false

The exact condition and affected fields should match the configuration implemented and tested in the ServiceNow instance.

6. UI Policy Actions

After creating the UI Policy, UI Policy Actions are configured for the required Incident fields.

Mandatory

When a field is marked as Mandatory, the user must provide a value before the form can be successfully submitted.

Example:

Mandatory = True

This helps prevent incomplete Incident records.

Read-only

When a field is marked as Read-only, the user cannot manually modify its value while the UI Policy condition is active.

Example:

Read-only = True

This helps protect important information from unwanted changes.

Visible

The Visible property controls whether a field is displayed on the Incident form.

Example:

Visible = True

A field can be shown or hidden depending on the configured UI Policy behavior.

7. Dynamic Behavior

The UI Policy provides dynamic behavior on the Incident form.

The general workflow is:

User opens Incident form
        ↓
Incident field values are checked
        ↓
UI Policy condition is evaluated
        ↓
Condition satisfied?
      /     \
    Yes      No
     ↓        ↓
UI Policy   Normal/
Actions     reversed
applied     behavior

When the condition becomes true, the configured UI Policy Actions are applied.

When the condition becomes false, the field behavior can be restored using the Reverse if false option where required.

