12. Limitations

The UI Policy mainly controls the behavior of fields on the client side.

It should be combined with appropriate Client Scripts and server-side validation when stronger data validation or business rules are required.

The actual behavior also depends on the conditions, fields, and UI Policy Actions configured in the ServiceNow instance.

13. Conclusion

The UI Policy implementation provides dynamic control over the ServiceNow Incident form. By using conditions and UI Policy Actions, fields can be made mandatory, read-only, or visible according to the required Incident situation.

The implementation works together with Client Scripts to improve form behavior, reduce data-entry errors, and maintain consistent Incident records.

The UI Policy was tested with different Incident scenarios to verify that the configured field behavior is applied correctly when the conditions are satisfied and restored when the conditions are no longer satisfied.

